Simon,

You didn't mention whether you are using OPL or C. Here is some OPL code
which I use which shows how to print to the destination set in the Psion system
screen "Printer configuration" dialog. After calling the procedure you can use
the standard OPL LPRINT command to print.

PROC einitp$:
	local a$(3),b%(6),r%,d%,f$(P_FNAMESIZE)
	a$="P$D"
	r%=call($218b,0,0,3,addr(b%()),uadd(addr(a$),1))
	if b%(1)=48
		lopen "par:a"
		f$="parallel port"
	elseif b%(1)=49
		lopen "tty:a"
		a$="P$S"
		r%=call($218b,0,0,3,addr(b%()),uadd(addr(a$),1))
		if r%=12
			iow(-1,7,b%(1),d%)
		endif
		f$="serial port"
	else
		a$="P$F"
		r%=call($218b,0,0,3,uadd(addr(f$),1),uadd(addr(a$),1))
		if r%>0 and r%<129
			pokeb addr(f$),r%
		else
			f$="\p.lis"
		endif
		lopen f$
	endif
	return f$
ENDP

Regards,

Andy